<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Barwe</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Shona kingdom of central Mozambique whose rulers, the Makombe, resisted Portuguese conquest into the 20th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Barwe emerged around 1500 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> lands and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-manyika">Kingdom of Manyika</a>, ruled by a dynasty related to the Mutapa house. Its rulers, titled Makombe, controlled routes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> and the gold-bearing highlands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Makombe was a sacred king whose installation required ritual approval, including holy water sent from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-uteve">Kingdom of Uteve</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spirit-medium">spirit mediums</a> held great influence. The kingdom traded with Portuguese posts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sena-mozambique">Sena</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tete">Tete</a> and frequently fought Afro-Portuguese prazo holders and neighbouring states. In the 19th century it fought off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaza-empire">Gaza Nguni</a> and the warlords of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After repeated campaigns, Portuguese forces occupied Barwe in 1902, ending its independence. A major rising in 1917, led by Barwe nobles and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spirit-medium">spirit mediums</a>, was crushed, and the area was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-mozambique">Portuguese Mozambique</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:8.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Shona religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Shona (Sena-Barwe)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mozambique">Mozambique</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Barue, Barwe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1701&amp;focus=kingdom-of-barwe" aria-label="Kingdom of Barwe on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5712 2700 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Barwe lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5833 3185h0M5861 3386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6032 2956h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6032 2956h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mozambique. <a href="/atlas?year=1701&amp;focus=kingdom-of-barwe">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
